      "text": "32,000 BCE  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n              │ CHAUVET CAVE (France)                                  │\n              │ Charcoal + ochre, sophisticated foreshortening         │\n              │ Rhinoceros, aurochs, horses in motion                  │\n              │ Panel of Lions — overlapping, suggesting depth         │\n              └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                    │\n  25,000 BCE  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n              │ VENUS FIGURINES (pan-European)                         │\n              │ Schematic female figures, exaggerated fertility markers │\n              │ Portable, not architectural — personal/ritual objects   │\n              └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                    │\n  17,000 BCE  ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n              │ LASCAUX CAVE (France)                                  │\n              │ Polychrome: black manganese + red/yellow ochre         │\n              │ Horses, aurochs, deer — registers, movement            │\n              └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                    │\n   3200 BCE   ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n              │ ANCIENT EGYPT                                          │\n              │ Canonic grid, frontality, hierarchical scale           │\n              │ Ka (soul) concept drives image function                │\n              │ Registers, hieroglyphs as image-text fusion            │\n              └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                    │\n    800 BCE   ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n              │ ANCIENT GREECE                                         │\n              │ Geometric → Archaic (kouros/kore) → Classical          │\n              │ (contrapposto, Polykleitos) → Hellenistic (pathos)     │\n              └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                    │\n    500 BCE   ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n              │ ANCIENT ROME                                           │\n              │ Portrait verism, triumphal relief continuity           │\n              │ Mosaic as medium, arch and vault enabling new space    │\n              └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```"
