        "id": "maxim:art-history:prehistoric-ancient",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "art-history",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[prehistoric, ancient]",
        "section": "art-history",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "01 - Prehistoric and Ancient Art",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**What they might be**: hunting magic, shamanic vision records, territorial markers,\nmyth narratives — all hypotheses. The fact that the same caves show evidence of use\nacross thousands of years suggests returning ritual practice, not casual marking.\nThe deep interior locations, inaccessible without light sources, reinforce deliberate\nceremonial access rather than casual decoration."
    }
